#!/bin/bash
# Personal website loop — self-paced; new session: /loop $(tail -1 PERSONAL_WEBSITE_LOOP.sh)
# Roadmap: docs/PERSONAL_WEBSITE_ROADMAP.md (doctrine §0, anchors §1, constraints §2, design system §3, approved claims §4, sections §5, ledger §6)
# Code lives in the nested repo personal-website/ (own remote, branch main). Deploy: vercel --prod from that dir.

Read docs/PERSONAL_WEBSITE_ROADMAP.md and follow its doctrine and hard rules exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task in Section 6; the task's spec text is the requirement and its Accept clause is the acceptance test. All code work happens in the nested repo personal-website/ (separate remote, branch main) — read the real files first (app/page.tsx, app/layout.tsx, app/globals.css, tailwind.config.js, package.json) before editing, never assume. TASTE: Section 0 bans the generic AI look (blue/purple gradient text, centered two-button hero, rounded-lg card grid with colored chips) — the existing page.tsx IS that look and gets replaced, not extended; Section 3 tokens are exact values, use them verbatim; premium comes from restraint (one accent, warm-white not #FFF, hairlines, tight negative tracking, grain), not from adding effects. TRUTH: every number rendered on the site must come from Section 4 Approved Claims or a live API response — never invent metrics, testimonials, logos, or press; if a section needs a number that isn't approved, verify it and add it to Section 4 first or leave the slot out. DEPENDENCY FLOOR: next/react/react-dom/tailwindcss only — no framer-motion, GSAP, lenis, three.js, shadcn, or icon packs; scroll animation is canvas + requestAnimationFrame, fonts are next/font; if a task feels like it needs a library you are over-building it. Every animation needs a prefers-reduced-motion branch, every fetch needs a cached/degraded path (PW-5's fallback JSON is mandatory — a previous attempt at live GitHub stats was reverted for fetching unguarded per-request). A task is done only when: npm run build is clean and npx tsc --noEmit is 0 errors (both from personal-website/), the task's Accept clause is actually checked (not assumed), the page renders at 390px and 1440px with zero horizontal overflow, and vercel --prod ran from personal-website/ (deploy straight to prod, never stage previews). Then flip the ledger line to [x], append ONE Section 7 Progress-log line with REAL numbers (build output sizes, route counts, Lighthouse scores from actual runs — no adjectives), commit in personal-website/ on main with message "feat(site): PW-n <what> — <verify numbers>" and commit the roadmap edit in the antigravity repo on roadmap/world-class (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). Never git push unless asked. PERSISTENCE: never end the loop on usage/rate limit or 429/overload — stop consuming tokens immediately, ScheduleWakeup 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger + Progress log and resume the same task from its last verified step (ledger + Progress log = recovery state); log partial progress BEFORE long/risky operations; chain hourly wakeups as many times as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining in Section 6, or a task blocked on user-only input (the portrait asset track, or Vercel Deployment Protection which is dashboard-only and currently 302-gating the prod URL) — then say exactly what's needed, ledger-note it, skip to the next unblocked [ ] task, and only if ALL remaining are blocked ScheduleWakeup 3600s so the loop resumes when unblocked.
